Interview Questions
Why synchronized?

Because number is shared by both threads.

Why while around wait()?

To re-check the condition after waking because of spurious wakeups or because another thread may have changed the shared state.

Why increment after printing?

Because the current thread has completed its turn and advances the shared state to the next number.

Why notifyAll() after increment?

Because the condition has changed. Waiting threads should wake up and check whether it is now their turn.

Why catch InterruptedException like this?
Thread.currentThread().interrupt();

This restores the thread's interrupted status instead of silently swallowing the interruption, allowing higher-level code to respond appropriately.

