public synchronized void printEven() {

    while (number <= limit) {

        while (number % 2 != 0) {

            try {

                wait();

            } catch (InterruptedException e) {

                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                return;

            }

        }

        if (number <= limit) {

            System.out.println(
                    Thread.currentThread().getName()
                    + " : "
                    + number);

            number++;

            notifyAll();

        }

    }

}

Notice one small improvement:

Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
return;

If the thread is interrupted, we restore the interrupt status and exit the method gracefully instead of continuing.

